angr opens libz3 itself: library_dir() takes the z3-solver wheel's bundled lib directory and
load() dlopen()s a fixed "libz3.so". Both halves are wrong on Arch. That directory does not
exist, because Arch packages z3-solver as Python files only and keeps the library in the
separate z3 package under a different soname, and the extension has a hard DT_NEEDED on
libz3.so.5.3, which no packaged z3 provides. Importing angr therefore dies with

    OSError: .../site-packages/z3/lib/libz3.so: cannot open shared object file

Carry the exact library angr was built against inside this package (angr/_z3lib, reached from
the extension through an $ORIGIN rpath) and prefer it, which also drops the requirement that a
z3 python module be importable at all: angr never imports z3, it only used find_spec to locate
the library. The cached directory holds just the versioned soname, so load() accepts that too.

The find_spec branch stays as the fallback, so behaviour is unchanged wherever the wheel's own
layout is present and this patch stops mattering once the repos ship z3-solver 5.3.3.0+.

diff --git a/angr/_z3.py b/angr/_z3.py
index f9a18aa..16f8fd6 100644
--- a/angr/_z3.py
+++ b/angr/_z3.py
@@ -23,7 +23,10 @@ else:
 
 
 def library_dir() -> Path:
-    """The lib directory of the installed z3-solver wheel. find_spec does not import the package."""
+    """The directory holding the libz3 that angr.rustylib links against."""
+    cached = Path(__file__).parent / "_z3lib"
+    if cached.is_dir():
+        return cached
     spec = importlib.util.find_spec("z3")
     if spec is None or spec.origin is None:
         raise ImportError("angr requires the z3-solver package, which does not appear to be installed")
@@ -32,4 +35,10 @@ def library_dir() -> Path:
 
 @functools.cache
 def load() -> ctypes.CDLL:
-    return ctypes.CDLL(library_dir() / LIBRARY_NAME)
+    directory = library_dir()
+    library = directory / LIBRARY_NAME
+    if not library.is_file():
+        versioned = sorted(directory.glob(f"{LIBRARY_NAME}.[0-9]*"))
+        if versioned:
+            library = versioned[0]
+    return ctypes.CDLL(library)
